ure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119361" :question/id #uuid "c4c8e89c-b26a-532f-8913-ca99a283c33a" :question/math-academy-id "q-119361" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +1+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1+({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-119361/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec62fd08-5729-5dc4-97b9-1a422f70109e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119361"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65225/selection/37e7d3213aea08fb68f2a1f14c6fcc1fc152125f6f4d94a6bbaf3b4e0ec55d7d" :answer/id #uuid "c309d3c7-c157-5466-a966-6243e92f1998" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65225/selection/fe86b03748aea2f31a748e72e1571f7bc040cda2d8cdb8f8d60443aee840091c" :answer/id #uuid "debf1862-f425-5935-9149-b6ae0226abac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q