+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }({sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-43293/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec62fd08-5729-5dc4-97b9-1a422f70109e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43293"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119367/selection/67107ebfcdbe0ebdc521c5b06e5ee4b90724dfcb9e66fca4b371e385a17ad7a6" :answer/id #uuid "20452ace-e4f8-5717-917d-19d12f9a4a08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119367/selection/a47b474639cc27ea1dde3df5e5126402385c1db6a2ffee364e6787d6df1721ac" :answer/id #uuid "106b8ed0-ad83-54d5-9101-a32f2631ea05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119367/selection/2b81853e2320e3a367352ecca066b6411b7d63f343505c393126e97bb3b18990" :answer/id #uuid "6bc6834c-6522-5d30-a831-c2b356b91403" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119367/selection/a75ab5ac470af66ffe449befeab1d734fb8b259d3482352912751c0a0245c5a9" :answer/id #uuid "7ee0dd13-ebc9-57cc-a016-c716e42eb7e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\op